 10, 2015 at 6:00:58 AM UTC-5, Andrew Yip wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hi guys, <div><br></div><div>I installed the current version of shiny-server on a ubuntu 14.04, and got the following during install:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:monospace;font-size:18px;line-height:24px;background-color:rgb(249,249,249)\"><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">sudo gdebi shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">server</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.759</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">amd64</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">deb</span></div></code></div></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:monospace;font-size:18px;line-height:24px;background-color:rgb(249,249,249)\">...</span></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Preparing</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> to unpack shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">server</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.759</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">amd64</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">deb </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Unpacking</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">server </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.759</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>dpkg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> error processing archive shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">server</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.759</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">amd64</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">deb </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(--</span><span style=\"color:#000\">install</span><span style=\"color:#660\">):</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> error creating directory </span><span style=\"color:#080\">`./opt/shiny-server&#39;: Permission denied<br>dpkg-deb: error: subprocess paste was killed by signal (Broken pipe)<br>Errors were encountered while processing:<br> shiny-server-1.4.1.759-amd64.deb</span></div></code></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(249,249,249)\"><font color=\"#555555\" face=\"monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;line-height:24px\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:monospace;font-size:18px;line-height:24px;background-color:rgb(249,249,249)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:white\">Would someone please shed some light on why there&#39;s a permission denial?</span><br></div><br><br>thank you <br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
